    <edge source="Person" target="Impaired Hypoglycaemia Awareness">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Impaired hypoglycaemia awareness exists when a person does not regularly sense the usual early warning symptoms of mild hypoglycaemia.</data>
      <data key="d9">absence,sensation,symptom</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-fbc891254df13760-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-fbc891254df13760</data>
      <data key="d12">1792687114</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Person" target="Driver Licensing Authority">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Driver Licensing Authority holds ultimate responsibility for issuing, renewing, suspending, or cancelling a person's driver licence.</data>
      <data key="d9">authority,licensing,responsibility</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-075c415b489fe411-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-075c415b489fe411</data>
      <data key="d12">1792687134</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Person" target="Health Professional">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">A person's fitness to drive is assessed by a Health Professional who evaluates medical criteria and potential impairments.</data>
      <data key="d9">fitness to drive,medical assessment</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-075c415b489fe411-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-075c415b489fe411</data>
      <data key="d12">1792687134</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Severe Hypoglycaemic Event" target="Impaired Hypoglycaemia Awareness">
      <data key="d7">3.0</data>
      <data key="d8">A severe hypoglycaemic event often leads to a temporary impaired hypoglycaemia awareness that must resolve before driving is permitted.&lt;SEP&gt;Rates of severe hypoglycaemia are up to seven times higher in individuals with impaired hypoglycaemia awareness compared to those who retain awareness.&lt;SEP&gt;The non-driving period following a severe hypoglycaemic event depends on the resolution of any temporary impaired hypoglycaemia awareness.</data>
      <data key="d9">cause,comparison,frequency,impairment,rate,resolution,temporary,temporary state</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-DM-COM-002-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-fbc891254df13760-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-DM-COM-002&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-fbc891254df13760</data>
      <data key="d12">1792687114</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Severe Hypoglycaemic Event" target="Glucose Control">
      <data key="d7">2.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The patterns of glucose control and behavior associated with a severe hypoglycaemic event take many weeks to re-establish.&lt;SEP&gt;After a severe hypoglycaemic event, it often takes many weeks for patterns of glucose control and behaviour to be re-established.</data>
      <data key="d9">pattern,re-establishment,recovery,time frame</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-DM-COM-002-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-fbc891254df13760-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-DM-COM-002&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-fbc891254df13760</data>
      <data key="d12">1792687114</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Severe Hypoglycaemic Event" target="Specialist">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">A specialist is required to urgently assess a person and provide recommendations on returning to driving based on the event.</data>
      <data key="d9">assessment,guidance,recommendation</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-DM-COM-002-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-DM-COM-002</data>
      <data key="d12">1792686904</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Severe Hypoglycaemic Event" target="Motor Vehicle Licence">
      <data key="d7">2.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The duration of the non-driving period following a severe hypoglycaemic event depends on factors including the type of motor vehicle licence held.&lt;SEP&gt;The specialist's recommendation for returning to driving after a severe hypoglycaemic event depends on the type of motor vehicle licence held.</data>
      <data key="d9">dependency,factor,recommendation,type,variation</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-DM-COM-002-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-fbc891254df13760-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-DM-COM-002&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-fbc891254df13760</data>
      <data key="d12">1792687114</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Severe Hypoglycaemic Event" target="Conditional Licence">
      <data key="d7">3.0</data>
      <data key="d8">A Conditional Licence requires that there is no recent history of a Severe Hypoglycaemic Event as assessed by the specialist.&lt;SEP&gt;There must be no recent history of a severe hypoglycaemic event as assessed by the specialist for a conditional licence.&lt;SEP&gt;There must be no recent history of a severe hypoglycaemic event, generally at least six weeks.</data>
      <data key="d9">assessment,criteria,exclusion,history,medical history,safety,six weeks</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-DM-COM-006-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-42507db0424f7a27-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-e3ca8efaf3d71461-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-DM-COM-006&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-42507db0424f7a27&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-e3ca8efaf3d71461</data>
      <data key="d12">1792687257</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Severe Hypoglycaemic Event" target="Driving">
      <data key="d7">2.0</data>
      <data key="d8">A severe hypoglycaemic event occurring while driving is a specific risk that the medical practitioner and person with diabetes aim to minimize.&lt;SEP&gt;A severe hypoglycaemic event is particularly relevant to driving because the loss of consciousness or seizure associated with such events poses significant risks during vehicle operation.</data>
      <data key="d9">occurrence,prevention,relevance,risk,safety</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-6c3afdfbb9a8da76-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-f16638e114f1fcde-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-6c3afdfbb9a8da76&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-f16638e114f1fcde</data>
      <data key="d12">1792687086</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Severe Hypoglycaemic Event" target="Hypoglycaemia">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">A severe hypoglycaemic event is defined as a specific instance or manifestation of the broader concept of hypoglycaemia that reaches a critical threshold.</data>
      <data key="d9">medical condition,severity</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-f16638e114f1fcde-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-f16638e114f1fcde</data>
      <data key="d12">1792687086</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Severe Hypoglycaemic Event" target="Blood Glucose">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The specialist's recommendation for returning to driving should be based on documented blood glucose over a reasonable interval.</data>
      <data key="d9">interval,measure,objective</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-fbc891254df13760-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-fbc891254df13760</data>
      <data key="d12">1792687114</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Severe Hypoglycaemic Event" target="Patient Survey">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The survey targets individuals who have experienced a severe hypoglycaemic event following a crash.</data>
      <data key="d9">context,history</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-457570d561f8a4dd-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-457570d561f8a4dd</data>
