    <edge source="Continuous Glucose Monitor" target="Individual">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Wearing a continuous glucose monitor is recommended to detect downward trends into the hypoglycaemia range.</data>
      <data key="d9">monitoring,safety alert</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-ad9a4415700efdab-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-ad9a4415700efdab</data>
      <data key="d12">1792687057</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Continuous Glucose Monitor" target="Hypoglycaemia Alert">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">A continuous glucose monitor preferably includes an active hypoglycaemia alert or alarm.</data>
      <data key="d9">feature,safety mechanism</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-ad9a4415700efdab-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-ad9a4415700efdab</data>
      <data key="d12">1792687057</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Flash Glucose Monitor" target="Individual">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Wearing a flash glucose monitor is recommended to detect downward trends into the hypoglycaemia range.</data>
      <data key="d9">monitoring,safety alert</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-ad9a4415700efdab-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-ad9a4415700efdab</data>
      <data key="d12">1792687057</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Vehicle" target="Individual">
      <data key="d7">4.0</data>
      <data key="d8">If mild hypoglycaemia symptoms occur while driving, the individual should turn off the engine and remove the keys from the ignition.&lt;SEP&gt;If mild hypoglycaemia symptoms occur while driving, the individual should safely steer the vehicle to the side of the road.&lt;SEP&gt;Driving is not recommenced until the individual feels well and at least 30 minutes after blood glucose is above 5 mmol/L.&lt;SEP&gt;Predicted glucose levels showing downward trends into the hypoglycaemia range are measured when the vehicle is parked.</data>
      <data key="d9">emergency response,measurement accuracy,parking,resumption criteria,safety check,safety procedure</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-ad9a4415700efdab-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-ad9a4415700efdab</data>
      <data key="d12">1792687057</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Snack" target="Individual">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Driving should not exceed two hours without considering having a snack to maintain glucose levels.</data>
      <data key="d9">prevention,timing</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-ad9a4415700efdab-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-ad9a4415700efdab</data>
      <data key="d12">1792687057</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Glucose" target="Individual">
      <data key="d7">2.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Mild hypoglycaemia is treated by self-administering glucose when symptoms occur while driving.&lt;SEP&gt;Adequate glucose must be carried in the vehicle for self-treatment of hypoglycaemia.</data>
      <data key="d9">administration,storage,treatment</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-ad9a4415700efdab-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-ad9a4415700efdab</data>
      <data key="d12">1792687057</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Self-Monitoring Blood Glucose Levels" target="Individual">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Blood glucose levels should be self-monitored before driving and every two hours during a journey.</data>
      <data key="d9">frequency,procedure</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-ad9a4415700efdab-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-ad9a4415700efdab</data>
      <data key="d12">1792687057</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Individual" target="Main Meal">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Delaying or missing a main meal is discouraged to prevent hypoglycaemia.</data>
      <data key="d9">nutrition,timing</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-ad9a4415700efdab-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-ad9a4415700efdab</data>
      <data key="d12">1792687057</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Comorbidities" target="People with diabetes">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The presence and management of comorbidities are a critical component in caring for individuals living with diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d9">assessment,health,management</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-bfabe371c5d42229-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-bfabe371c5d42229</data>
      <data key="d12">1792687064</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Comorbidities" target="Fitness to drive">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Evaluating comorbidities directly influences the determination of a person's fitness to drive.</data>
      <data key="d9">assessment,driving safety,management</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-bfabe371c5d42229-chunk-000</data>
